# Tests that CUE_UPDATE keeps an @test(eq:todo) that matches in source order
# but fails under a non-source @test(permute) ordering. The expectation
# checks field order, so it holds for a-then-b but not for b-then-a.
#
# Without the gate, the update would promote the todo to @test(eq, ...) on
# the strength of the source ordering alone, and the re-run would fail
# under the permutation (the update would not be idempotent).
-- in/test.cue --
s: {
	@test(permute, count=2)
	a: 1
	b: 2
} @test(eq:todo, {@test(checkOrder), a: 1, b: 2})
-- out/status.txt --
update: identical to input
force:  identical to update
